  "comment": "The object-oriented surface over the natives (docs/language.md, \"Members\"; docs/research/oo-surface.md). tools/gen-members.cs writes src/Ffx.Atel.Game/Members.g.cs from this file and data/natives.json; the compiler lowers each member onto its native, and the decompiler writes the member where the bytes allow. \"groups\": the containers members go into: \"component\" (a property of every worker, Turn.Start()), \"indexed\" (a property of every worker indexed by the native's first argument, Sprites[3].Show(…)), \"static\" (an engine-wide static class, Wait.Frames(…)); a group whose name has a dot is a static group nested in the one before the dot (\"Camera.Eye\": Camera.Eye.AimAt(…)). \"members\": native id -> \"member\" (a path: \"Pos\" a member of the worker, \"Turn.Start\" a member of a group, \"Camera.Eye.AimAt\" a member of a nested group, \"Pos.X\" a component of a Vector3 property), \"as\" (\"method\", the default; \"get\" or \"set\" for a property), \"worker\" (the native's first argument is the worker it acts on: unqualified the member passes Common.GetWorkerId(-1), Tidus.Member passes Tidus's number, Workers[n].Member passes n), \"vector\" (the setter's three float arguments are a Vector3), \"bool\" (the setter's value is 0 or 1: a bool property). Names come from the native's verified name and its summary; a member names nothing the native's documentation does not say.",
  "groups": {
    "Turn": {
      "kind": "component",
      "type": "TurnControl",
      "summary": "The worker's turn: set it up (<see cref=\"TurnControl.Yaw\"/>, <see cref=\"TurnControl.SetFrames\"/>), start it (<see cref=\"TurnControl.Start\"/>), wait for it (<see cref=\"TurnControl.Wait\"/>)."
    },
    "Move": {
      "kind": "component",
      "type": "MoveControl",
      "summary": "The worker's move: set it up (<see cref=\"MoveControl.Target\"/>, <see cref=\"MoveControl.Speed\"/>), start it (<see cref=\"MoveControl.Start\"/>), wait for it (<see cref=\"MoveControl.Wait\"/>)."
    },
    "Motion": {
      "kind": "component",
      "type": "MotionControl",
      "summary": "The motion of the worker's model. Assign a motion id to set it (<c>Motion = 0x71050;</c>, <c>Chr.SetMotion</c>); its members play, wait for and release motions."
    },
    "Neck": {
      "kind": "component",
      "type": "NeckControl",
      "summary": "The neck of the worker's model: where it looks and how fast it turns there."
    },
    "Sprites": {
      "kind": "indexed",
      "type": "SpriteList",
      "item": "Sprite",
      "summary": "The screen's sprites by slot (0-127): <c>Sprites[3].Show(V12)</c>."
    },
    "Wait": {
      "kind": "static",
      "summary": "Waiting: frames, for ever."
    },
    "Camera": {
      "kind": "static",
      "summary": "The camera: its eye (<see cref=\"Camera.Eye\"/>), the point it looks at (<see cref=\"Camera.Focus\"/>), the screens it draws to (<see cref=\"Camera.Screen\"/>), roll, screen depth and blur."
    },
    "Camera.Eye": {
      "kind": "static",
      "summary": "The camera's eye (side 1 of its channel, FFX.exe's <c>cam</c>): where it is, how it moves there, its limits, path and shakes."
    },
    "Camera.Focus": {
      "kind": "static",
      "summary": "The point the camera looks at (side 0 of its channel, FFX.exe's <c>ref</c>): where it is, how it moves there, its limits, path and shakes."
    },
    "Camera.Screen": {
      "kind": "static",
      "summary": "The screens the camera draws to, by number (<c>MsScreen…</c>): their shakes and moves."
    },
    "Sound": {
      "kind": "static",
      "summary": "Sound effects."
    },
    "Voice": {
      "kind": "static",
      "summary": "The voice line: prepare it (<see cref=\"Voice.Prepare\"/>), play it (<see cref=\"Voice.Play\"/>), wait while it plays (<see cref=\"Voice.IsPlaying\"/>), stop it."
    }
  },
